The injection of D₀ into the product of D₀ and D₁ relates X to W when X is a neighbourhood of D₀, W is a product neighbourhood, and the product neighbourhood of X with the master of D₁ is contained in W. Domain and codomain membership are the first two conjuncts. The masters are related by a reflexive inclusion. An intersection on the right is a product neighbourhood by the product intersection law, and the two inclusions combine. If X' lies below X and W lies below W', the product neighbourhood of X' with the master lies below that of X, and the inclusions compose.
